From 608e1ee8cfa4ddb94b993817dfdf079feb3ce988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vogel <jvogel@stygian.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:28:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] asuran-cli/src/contents.rs: disambiguate import of struct
 Manifest

Building with current rust produces this error:
---
error: `Manifest` is ambiguous
  --> asuran-cli/src/contents.rs:16:24
   |
16 |     let mut manifest = Manifest::load(&repo);
   |                        ^^^^^^^^ ambiguous name
   |
   = note: ambiguous because of multiple glob imports of a name in the same module
note: `Manifest` could refer to the struct imported here
  --> asuran-cli/src/contents.rs:3:5
   |
 3 | use asuran::manifest::*;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: consider adding an explicit import of `Manifest` to disambiguate
note: `Manifest` could also refer to the struct imported here
  --> asuran-cli/src/contents.rs:4:5
   |
 4 | use asuran::prelude::*;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: consider adding an explicit import of `Manifest` to disambiguate
   = warning: this was previously accepted by the compiler but is being phased out; it will become a hard error in a future release!
   = note: for more information, see issue #114095 <https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/114095>
   = note: `#[deny(ambiguous_glob_imports)]` (part of `#[deny(future_incompatible)]`) on by default
---
Fix by explicit import of Manifest with 'use asuran::manifest::Manifest;'.
---
 asuran-cli/src/contents.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/asuran-cli/src/contents.rs b/asuran-cli/src/contents.rs
index 642a15f..f8716ec 100644
--- a/asuran-cli/src/contents.rs
+++ b/asuran-cli/src/contents.rs
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 use crate::cli::*;
 
 use asuran::manifest::*;
+use asuran::manifest::Manifest;
 use asuran::prelude::*;
 
 use anyhow::{anyhow, Result};
-- 
2.56.0

